{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "931fa049-26e6-4ec9-b86c-1e3fbeef4d8d",
    "name": "ACME Salary Management — API Collection",
    "schema": "https://schema.postman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "All 14 APIs from docs/api-conventions.md. There are 15 requests because CSRF is fetched before login and refreshed afterward.\n\nKeep Postman's cookie jar enabled. Run 01–03 to sign in, then select the requests you want to exercise. Logout is last. JSON writes include the refreshed CSRF header. The collection runner stops on HTTP errors and does not automatically retry credentials or writes.\n\nRequests 09–14 demonstrate a stateful workflow using a separate managedEmployeeId: create an employee, update details, record a salary change, inspect history, estimate monthly base pay, then mark the employee inactive. These requests modify data when the corresponding endpoints are available. The employeeId variable used by requests 07–08 is separate from managedEmployeeId. Choose a new unique managedEmployeeId and managedEmployeeEmail before creating another employee.\n\nCreate/details/status success responses update employeeVersion. Review the employee and version before manual writes. Version conflicts are never automatically resolved. Employee creation has no deduplication contract; reconcile by employee ID before retrying an uncertain create.\n\nFor a new salary operation, clear salaryOperationKey. Its script generates a UUID once and captures the resolved request body. Retries with that key send the exact same saved body, including its original version. To change intent, clear salaryOperationKey and edit the salary body before sending. Success/replay does not replace the version of its original operation.\n\nCollection variables include the documented local demo login, sample employee data, salary amount/effective date, and estimate month. Adjust dates and values for the records you are testing. Report/list optional filters are disabled Params that can be enabled; repeat keys for multiple values rather than comma-packed lists. Money is sent as decimal strings. No live session or CSRF tokens are embedded."
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Backend origin, without a trailing slash."
    },
    {
      "key": "email",
      "value": "maya.rao@acme.example",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Enabled local demo HR email."
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "AcmeDev!2026",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Documented local demo password."
    },
    {
      "key": "csrfToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Populated by the CSRF requests; do not enter a constant token."
    },
    {
      "key": "employeeId",
      "value": "EMP-000001",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Detail lookup ID; updated from the first item returned by the employee list."
    },
    {
      "key": "managedEmployeeId",
      "value": "EMP-010001",
